# Grid A — S3D Config trace, schema-level absence (no sibling fallback)
#
# Targets: config_trace scenario + ReqConfigMapping + ShapeExplanation
# under conditions where the LLM CANNOT find a useful sibling key. Pins
# the 2026-05+ scope-axis migration: when no per-line sibling cite is
# available, the answer surface depends on the LLM emitting schema-
# level evidence (scope=file for layer-canonical files, scope=negative
# for the absence proof, scope=crossfile for "no CLI flag for this
# group" attestation).
#
# The phantom key `explore_xyz_phantom_unique_budget` is intentionally
# distinctive enough that no real key will sibling-match it: there is
# no `explore_xyz_*` family in either codrax.yaml or RuntimeSettings,
# so the LLM can't escape into a sibling-line cite. It MUST either
# (a) emit schema-level evidence to anchor the absence + the layers
# structurally, or (b) leave the answer surface thin (one-layer prose
# only — fails the multi-anchor expectation).
#
# Ground truth: explore_* group is yaml-only (no CLI override flag),
# the canonical config layer is codrax.yaml, the default-struct layer
# is internal/types/config.go (DefaultExploreHeuristics), and the
# phantom key does not exist in any layer.
#
# Eval gate: EXPECT_CONTAINS / EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS / EXPECT_SECTIONS
# verify the answer surfaces all three layers AND mentions the
# absence explicitly. The answer doesn't need to LITERALLY say
# "scope=file" — it needs to ground each layer with a citable anchor
# (which is what schema-level scopes structurally enable).
ID="s3d"
NAME="config trace — phantom-key precedence with schema-level absence"
QUESTION="explore_xyz_phantom_unique_budget 在三层覆盖（默认值 / codrax.yaml / CLI flag）里各自的有效值是什么？给我每一层的来源锚点。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="codrax.yaml DefaultExploreHeuristics"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="explore_xyz_phantom_unique_budget = 5 默认值是 5 默认值是 6"
EXPECT_SECTIONS="codrax.yaml DefaultExploreHeuristics"
